```

But `readOptionalString` throwing error caught by outer catch; we can return 400 via status. Use `throw Object.assign(new Error(...), { status: 400 })`. Good.
For `nameValue === null`, return 400.
For `bioValue === null`, treat as empty -> null.
For avatar/banner null -> clear.
For contact fields null -> clear.
For `contactVisibility` null -> 400.
Also prevent changing `username`, `role`, `email`, `password`, etc. by ignoring unknown fields. Good.
Potential admin body username: if body username is not string (object), readOptionalString only used for fields; bodyUsername check typeof. Good.
`profanityFilter.clean` can return string. Fine.
`patch` type is Record<string, any>; storage update type accepts. Fine.
`normalizeEmail` already imported. Good.

One nuance: `sanitizeProfileBio` preserves newlines; `profanityFilter.clean` regex with words works across. Fine.
`validateAvatarUrl` now rejects unknown hosts. The existing profile edit in UserProfile uploads to Cloudinary, so okay. But Google avatars are googleusercontent. Good.
`validateBannerUrl` same.
`validateContactWebsite` allows any public https. Good.
`isValidContactEmail` rejects uppercase? It normalizes lower. Fine.
`isValidContactPhone` checks sanitized string. Good.

Also maybe require contact visibility not public if no contact? Not necessary.
Also update `contactVisibility` default when contact fields set and no visibility? Keep private by default.

Let's apply.

