content.text:
Now update UserProfile.tsx to show banner/contact and link to /profile. Let's plan exact edits.

1. Interface add bannerUrl, contact, contactVisibility.
2. Remove inline editing states? Let's decide. I'll simplify: remove `editing`, `bio`, `name`, `saving`, `avatarRef`? But we still need `isOwn`. We can keep avatar quick upload? The new profile page handles. Let's remove inline edit form and avatar upload, and change button to Link. But removing `Textarea`, `Pencil` imports etc. Let's implement cleanly.

Current imports:
```tsx
import { createElement, useCallback, useEffect, useRef, useState } from "react";
import { Link, useLocation, useParams } from "wouter";
import { ArrowLeft, Ban, Calendar, Flag, Loader2, MessageCircle, Pencil, UserMinus, UserPlus, X } from "lucide-react";
import Navbar...
import { Button }...
import { Textarea }...
```
We'll need `Mail`, `Phone`, `Globe`, `Pencil` maybe for edit button, `Link` already. Remove `useRef`, `Textarea`, `avatarRef`, etc.

But maybe keep `uploadAvatar` for convenience? The new page is accessible via "Editar perfil". If we remove, less code. Let's remove.

New interface:
```tsx
contact?: {
  email?: string | null;
  phone?: string | null;
  website?: string | null;
} | null;
contactVisibility?: "public" | "followers" | "private" | string | null;
bannerUrl?: string | null;
```

Remove `bio`, `name`, `saving`, `editing`, `avatarRef`, `saveProfile`, `uploadAvatar`. Keep `profile` etc.

Render section:
```tsx
<section className="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/50 bg-card">
  <div className="relative h-36 w-full bg-gradient-to-r from-primary/30 via-primary/10 to-transparent sm:h-48">
    {profile.bannerUrl ? <img src={profile.bannerUrl} alt="" className="h-full w-full object-cover" /> : null}
  </div>
  <div className="p-6 pt-0 space-y-4">
    <div className="-mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-end gap-4">
      <div className="h-24 w-24 ...">avatar</div>
      <div className="flex-1 space-y-1 sm:pb-1">
        <h1>...</h1>
        ...
      </div>
    </div>
    <p bio>...
    {contact...}
    <div actions>
      {isOwn ? <Link href="/profile"><Button><Pencil/> Editar perfil</Button></Link> : ...}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
```
Note: `profile.isBlocked` and `isBlockedBy` should hide contact. The server already hides contact if blocked, but UI can hide. Fine.

Contact rendering:
```tsx
{profile.contact && (profile.contact.email || profile.contact.phone || profile.contact.website) && (
  <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2 pt-1">
    {profile.contact.email && <a href={`mailto:${profile.contact.email}`} className="..."><Mail .../> {profile.contact.email}</a>}
    {profile.contact.phone && <a href={`tel:${profile.contact.phone.replace(/[^\d+]/g, "")}`} ...><Phone/> {profile.contact.phone}</a>}
    {profile.contact.website && <a href={profile.contact.website} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ...><Globe/> {new URL(profile.contact.website).hostname.replace(/^www\./,"")}</a>}
  </div>
)}
```
`new URL` could throw if malformed, but server validated. To be safe, compute `websiteLabel`:
```tsx
const websiteLabel = (() => { try { return new URL(profile.contact!.website!).hostname.replace(/^www\./,""); } catch { return profile.contact!.website!; } })();
```
Could just show "Sitio web" text. Simpler: show `profile.contact.website.replace(/^https?:\/\//, "").split("/")[0]`. Safe. Use that.

If isOwn and no contact:
```tsx
{isOwn && profile.contactVisibility !== "public" && !profile.contact && (
  <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Tu información de contacto está oculta. <Link href="/profile" className="text-primary-ink underline">Configúrala aquí</Link>.</p>
)}
```
But if contactVisibility private and contact exists, server returns null for owner? Wait, isOwner true => canViewContact true, so owner sees contact. So `profile.contact` is not null for own even if private. Good. If no contact at all, show prompt.

Actions: for own, `Link href="/profile"` with Button "Editar perfil". For others, follow/message/block/report. Keep.

Let's edit imports and states first.

